---
title: Docker Installation
description: Run FOSSBilling with Docker for a consistent, isolated environment.
---

{% aside type="tip" %}
New to Docker? It packages apps with all their dependencies, so they run the same way everywhere. No more "it works on my machine" problems. [Learn more about containers](https://www.docker.com/resources/what-container/).
{% /aside %}

## Prerequisites

- [Docker Engine](https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/) installed on your system

## Choose Your Setup

{% aside %}
We use the `latest` tag for stable releases. Change to `preview` for bleeding-edge versions, or specify a version number like `0.6.0`.
{% /aside %}

{% tabs %}
{% tabitem label="Standalone" %}
Simplest option — runs FOSSBilling alone. You'll need an external database.

```bash
docker run -d -p 80:80 \
  -v fossbilling:/var/www/html \
  --restart=always \
  fossbilling/fossbilling:latest
```

Then visit your server IP/hostname in a browser to complete the web installer.
{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="Docker Compose" %}
Complete stack with MySQL included. Best for getting started quickly.

```yaml
version: "3.9"
services:
  fossbilling:
    image: fossbilling/fossbilling:latest
    restart: always
    ports:
      - 80:80
    volumes:
      - fossbilling:/var/www/html

  mysql:
    image: mysql:8.2
    restart: always
    environment:
      MYSQL_DATABASE: fossbilling
      MYSQL_USER: fossbilling
      MYSQL_PASSWORD: fossbilling
      MYSQL_RANDOM_ROOT_PASSWORD: '1'
    volumes:
      - mysql:/var/lib/mysql

volumes:
  fossbilling:
  mysql:
```

Run it:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

First startup downloads images — this may take a few minutes.

**Database credentials** (if using the example above):
- Hostname: `mysql`
- Database: `fossbilling`
- Username: `fossbilling`
- Password: `fossbilling`

Access the installer at `http://localhost` (or your server IP/hostname).
{% /tabitem %}
{% /tabs %}

## Post-Installation

{% aside type="danger" %}
**Cron is required.** FOSSBilling won't work properly without it.
{% /aside %}

After installation, set up the cron job on your host:

```bash
(crontab -l; echo "*/5 * * * * docker exec <container-name/id> su www-data -s /usr/local/bin/php /var/www/html/cron.php") | awk '!x[$0]++' | crontab -
```

Find your container name/ID:

```bash
docker ps
```

